<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Fintech yr earnings jump, order books high.</title>
<headline>Fintech yr earnings jump, order books high.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended Feb 28, 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)   564.7	 vs 449.4</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     631.1	 vs 449.4</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 185.0	 vs 150.0</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   76.03	 vs 53.76</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   102.19	vs 74.65</p>
<p>    Tax			 25.43	 vs 20.07</p>
<p>    Interest received     0.29	  vs 1.05 paid</p>
<p>    Exceptional gain	6.69	  vs  -</p>
<p>    Turnover		  973.11	vs 954.96</p>
<p>Div payable June 2</p>
<p>on register May 23</p>
<p>Full name: Fintech Ltd (electronics and electrical)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said order books remained at a high level. The exceptional gain reflected profits on the disposal of 50 percent of XeraTech.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
